    {
      "sectionId": "section-dark-gift-feats",
      "parentSectionId": "section-dnd-55-origin-feat-guides",
      "heading": "Dark Gift Feats",
      "sourceAnchor": "dark-gift-feats",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-dark-gift-feats-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Dark Gift feats were introduced in Ravenloft: The Horrors Within, and specify that they require a Ravenloft campaign. Whether you’re playing in Ravenloft or not, they have some unique mechanics. First, with DM permission, you can take a Dark Gift any time that you would otherwise receive an Origin Feat. Second, each Dark Gift causes something horrible to happen to you when you roll a 1 on a D20 Test. Dark Gifts frequently have comparable Origin Feats, but add more power in exchange for the additional risk."
            }
          ]
